# React Query Rules - Watfil Project

## General Rules

React Query is the single source of truth for all server state.

Always use:

- useQuery
- useMutation
- useInfiniteQuery
- useQueryClient

Never use:

- Redux for API data
- Context API for API data
- useEffect + useState for fetching
- fetch API

Always use Axios instance from:

```text
shared/api/axios.js
```

---

## Architecture Flow

Always follow:

```text
Component
    ↓
Custom Hook
    ↓
Repository
    ↓
Axios Instance
    ↓
Backend API
```

Never skip layers.

Bad:

```jsx
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryFn: () => axios.get("/products"),
});
```

Good:

```jsx
const { data } = useProducts();
```

---

## Repository Pattern

Each feature must contain an api folder.

Example:

```text
features/products/api
```

Repository example:

```js
export const ProductRepository = {
  getAll: (params) => api.get("/company/products", { params }),

  getById: (id) => api.get(`/company/products/${id}`),

  create: (data) => api.post("/company/products", data),

  update: (id, data) => api.post(`/company/products/${id}`, data),

  delete: (id) => api.delete(`/company/products/${id}`),
};
```

Never call Axios directly inside components.

---

## Query Key Factory Pattern

Every feature must have query keys.

Example:

```js
export const productKeys = {
  all: ["products"],

  lists: () => [...productKeys.all, "list"],

  list: (filters) => [...productKeys.lists(), filters],

  details: () => [...productKeys.all, "detail"],

  detail: (id) => [...productKeys.details(), id],
};
```

Never hardcode query keys inside hooks.

Bad:

```js
["products"]["orders"];
```

Good:

```js
productKeys.list(filters);
productKeys.detail(id);
```

---

## Query Defaults

Use centralized query options from queryClient.

Default values:

```js
{
  staleTime: 5 * 60 * 1000,
  retry: 1,
  refetchOnWindowFocus: false,
  refetchOnReconnect: true,
}
```

Do not redefine these values in every query unless necessary.

---

## Query Hooks

Every query must be wrapped inside a custom hook.

Example:

```js
export function useProducts(filters) {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: productKeys.list(filters),

    queryFn: () => ProductRepository.getAll(filters),

    select: (response) => response.data.data,
  });
}
```

Never use useQuery directly inside pages.

Never use useQuery directly inside presentational components.

---

## Conditional Queries

Always use enabled when query depends on dynamic values.

Example:

```js
enabled: Boolean(productId);
```

Bad:

```js
useQuery({
  queryKey: ["product", id],
  queryFn: () => getProduct(id),
});
```

Good:

```js
useQuery({
  queryKey: productKeys.detail(id),
  queryFn: () => getProduct(id),
  enabled: Boolean(id),
});
```

---

## Mutation Hooks

All mutations must be isolated in custom hooks.

Example:

```js
export function useCreateProduct() {
  const queryClient = useQueryClient();

  return useMutation({
    mutationFn: ProductRepository.create,

    onSuccess: () => {
      queryClient.invalidateQueries({
        queryKey: productKeys.all,
      });
    },
  });
}
```

Never place mutation logic inside components.

---

## Cache Invalidation Rules

After Create:

```js
queryClient.invalidateQueries({
  queryKey: productKeys.all,
});
```

After Update:

```js
queryClient.invalidateQueries({
  queryKey: productKeys.all,
});

queryClient.invalidateQueries({
  queryKey: productKeys.detail(id),
});
```

After Delete:

```js
queryClient.invalidateQueries({
  queryKey: productKeys.all,
});
```

Always keep cache synchronized with backend state.

---

## Data Selection

Normalize API responses inside hooks using select.

Bad:

```jsx
const products = data?.data?.data?.items ?? [];
```

Good:

```js
select: (response) => response.data.data;
```

Components should never know backend response structure.

---

## Watfil API Response Shape

Lists:

```json
{
  "data": [],
  "meta": {}
}
```

Single Resource:

```json
{
  "data": {}
}
```

Mutations:

```json
{
  "message": "",
  "data": {}
}
```

Always normalize responses inside hooks.

Never expose raw Axios responses to UI.

---

## Pagination Pattern

Laravel APIs return:

```json
{
  "data": [],
  "meta": {
    "total": 0,
    "current_page": 1,
    "last_page": 1,
    "per_page": 15
  }
}
```

Keep pagination metadata.

Never discard meta.

Preferred return shape:

```js
{
  items: response.data.data,
  meta: response.data.meta,
}
```

---

## Infinite Query Rules

Use useInfiniteQuery only when API supports cursor-based or page-based loading.

Do not use useInfiniteQuery for standard admin tables.

Default to paginated useQuery.

---

## Loading States

Every page must handle:

- loading state
- empty state
- error state
- success state

Expose:

```js
isLoading;
isPending;
isFetching;
isError;
```

Never assume data exists.

---

## Error Handling

Always handle API errors.

Use:

```js
onError;
```

or

```js
try/catch
```

Map errors to user-friendly messages.

Never expose raw backend messages directly.

Never silently ignore failed requests.

---

## Optimistic Updates

Allowed:

- likes
- ratings
- simple UI toggles

Not allowed:

- orders
- wallet transactions
- withdrawals
- topups
- financial operations

Always wait for backend confirmation for business-critical actions.

---

## Redux Integration

Redux Toolkit is only allowed for:

- auth
- theme
- language
- sidebar
- ui state
- global filters

Never store:

- products
- orders
- wallet
- customers
- catalog
- company profile

inside Redux.

These belong to React Query.

---

## Folder Structure

Every feature must follow:

```text
feature
│
├── api
│   └── featureRepository.js
│
├── hooks
│   ├── useEntities.js
│   ├── useEntity.js
│   ├── useCreateEntity.js
│   ├── useUpdateEntity.js
│   └── useDeleteEntity.js
│
├── constants
│   └── featureQueryKeys.js
│
├── components
├── pages
├── schemas
└── types
```

Use the real feature name for generic feature-layer files:

```text
features/products/api/productsRepository.js
features/products/constants/productsQueryKeys.js
```

